Case 
 Help > Transaction > Case Management" />
 Case 
 &#160; 
 This 
 interface allows the Customer Support Agent to create a case or ticket 
 for a complaint raised by a customer. Once a case has been raised and 
 allocated to a support agent, the support agent will further assign the 
 case to internal team member or external vendors for resolution. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Business 
 Unit : Select 
 the Business Unit of the customer from the list fetched from Business 
 Unit master. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Financial 
 Year : Select the Financial 
 Year, by default current year will be auto selected 
 &#160; 
 Document 
 Type : Select the type of document from the dropdown list 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Document 
 Date : Select the date, by default will be the current date 
 &#160; 
 Document 
 No : This is auto generated when the entry is saved 
 &#160; 
 Reference : Select the case 
 reference from the dropdown list “Booking” or “Payment FollowUp” 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Reference 
 Details 
 &#160; 
 Customer : 
 Select the customer from the 
 list fetched from the Customer database 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Unit : Unit is auto fetched 
 when the customer is selected 
 &#160; 
 Email : &#160; &#160;Email 
 is auto fetched when the customer is selected 
 &#160; 
 Mobile : Mobile number is 
 auto fetched when the customer is selected 
 &#160; 
 Note: There is masking facility against the 
 customer’s Mobile number and E-mail id 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Case 
 Details 
 &#160; 
 Case 
 Hierarchy : Select the hierarchy 
 of the case from the dropdown menu 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Parent case : This option 
 will be enabled only when the type is selected as Child. Where user can 
 select a parent case from the list to create a hierarchy 
 &#160; 
 Type : 
 Select the type of the case from the dropdown list 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Status : Select the status 
 from the dropdown menu “Open” or “Closed” 
 &#160; 
 CS Executive : Select the 
 Customer Support Executive who attended the customer case 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Origin : Select the origin 
 of the case from the dropdown list 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Priority : Select the Priority 
 of the case from the list 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Remarks : Type the Subject 
 of the case 
 &#160; 
 Reason Information 
 &#160; 
 Reason : Select the reason 
 of this case entry from the dropdown menu 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Sub Reason : Select the Sub 
 Reason from the dropdown list 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Sub Reason Property :Select 
 the Sub Reason property from the dropdown list 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Attachment 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Add 
 New Row : Select 
 this option to attach a supporting document for the case described in 
 the entry 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Click and browse 
 for adding the supporting document from the file uploader pop up 
 &#160; 
 Remove Row : 
 Select the Attachments and click this option to remove the attachments 
 you have added by mistake 
 &#160; 
 Click 
 on submit to save the transaction 
 &#160; 
 Task 
 &#160; 
 Open 
 the case from the Advance search, go to task, here user can find all the 
 tasks created against the case in a listed manner. 
 &#160; 
 Option 
 to convert the task into an activity is available as shown below. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Activity 
 &#160; 
 This 
 tab shows all the activities completed against this specific case with 
 the remarks. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 All Email Communication 
 &#160; 
 This 
 tab shows details of email communications. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 Advance Search 
 &#160; 
 User can 
 search by Document No, Booking No, Document Date, Business Unit, Customer, 
 Unit, Status etc. 
 &#160; 
 Example 
 &#160; 
 User can 
 see all the closed cases from Case Advance Search page. 
 &#160; 
 Put the 
 value close in search box for Status and hit enter key. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 All the 
 closed Cases will be shown in Advance Search page. 
 &#160; 
 Attached file 
 name is shown when the attachment is done in Case Activity. 
 In Case Advance Search page Select the Activity 
 from triple bar icon . Select 
 'Activity Type' email and click on 'Attachment'. 
 Select the file and click on upload File. Name 
 of attached file is shown in the Case Activity page. 
 &#160; 
 View the content 
 of email sent from Case Activity 
 &#160; 
 Go to Case 
 Advance Search page. 
 &#160; 
 Click on 
 the case to open it, and then click on All Email Communication to open. 
 &#160; 
 All the 
 email contents are showing in chronological order. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 User can add 
 multiple attachments from Email Case Activity 
 &#160; 
 Go to Case 
 Management > Case > Case Advance Search. 
 &#160; 
 Select the 
 Case and open in view mode. 
 &#160; 
 Select Activity 
 option from triple bar in right side. Select the Activity Type email. 
 &#160; 
 Select the 
 Template -> Click on Attachment icon -> Select multiple files and 
 required data and submit. 
 &#160; 
 All the 
 attached files will be sent through email to selected Email Ids. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 To 
 view the status of all Tasks created for a Case 
 &#160; 
 Steps: 
 1. &#160;&#160; Log in to Farvision. 
 2. &#160;&#160; Go to Case 
 Management > Case 
 > Advance Search 
 3. &#160;&#160; Zoom into the Case 
 and go to Task tab. 
 &#160; 
 Expected 
 Result: The Converted status, 
 as well as the Converted Date 
 and Converted Time for each 
 task are displayed in the grid. 
 &#160; 
 &#160; 
 To v iew CS Agent's 
 Name in Activity tab under Case 
 &#160; 
 Steps: 
 1. &#160;&#160;&#160; Log in to Farvision 
 2. &#160;&#160;&#160; Go to Case 
 Management > Case 
 > Advance Search 
 3. &#160;&#160;&#160; Zoom into the Case and go to Activity 
 tab 
 &#160; 
 Expected 
 Result: Identify the CS agent who performed each activity by checking 
 the newly added Activity 
 Done By field. 
 &#160; 
